    "b-00-overview-decision-card-chrom-15": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-decision-card-chrom-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Card chrome (cap kind, group, side, style) is resolved once in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "trace-viewer/SpanCard/SpanCard.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and threaded to variants as a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "SpanCardChrome",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " bundle; variants ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "SpanCard/variants/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") supply content only.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Per-variant chrome (rejected) is how row anatomies drift apart. A new variant gets the standard frame for free and cannot opt out.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "SpanCard/variants/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", including variants not yet written."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-decision-the-card-t-17": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-decision-the-card-t-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Each trace-tree and detail-panel constant has exactly one owner module, listed below with the test that pins it.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": The design page's invariants (three sizes, fixed 24px cells, square caps) then have one place to be violated and, where pinned, one test to catch it. Ad-hoc local constants were the rejected default.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": all trace-tree and detail-panel rendering code."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
