    "b-00-overview-decision-trace-vie-16": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-decision-trace-vie-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Every surface that shows role or kind color resolves it through the icon resolver (table above), the detail panel's message stream included.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Duplicated hue tables (rejected) are how the tree and the panel stop agreeing on what blue means.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "icons/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and any new surface rendering span identity."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-decision-detail-ren-18": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-decision-detail-ren-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Detail renderers are data-only functions in the exported renderer registry (table above), and the conformance test iterates the registry rather than a hand-kept list. The renderer contract and the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "DetailBlockProvider",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " host seam are defined in the Viewer Model; their types live in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "detail-panel/contract.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "detail-panel/blocks.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ".\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": A renderer added later is covered without touching the test, so the contract enforces itself on unwritten code. A manually maintained test list was the rejected alternative.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "detail-panel/renderers/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", every future renderer and extension block source."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-decision-detail-pa-19": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-decision-detail-pa-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "detail-panel/doc-figure/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the single data-block substrate app-wide (figure, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "tokenize.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Clamped.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "); JSON canonicalization sits beside the renderers ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "renderers/json-document.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), and the primary-figure clamp constant is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "renderers/primary-figure.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", stamped by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "renderers/TurnBody.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ".\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Byte-exactness, gutter, zebra, and clamp behavior are contracts (design page); one substrate means one place they can break. Per-surface code blocks were the rejected pattern.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": any surface rendering source text, including future tabs and renderers, which inherit the primary-figure policy from the Turn body rather than naming it."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-decision-viewer-ui-20": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-decision-viewer-ui-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": viewer-ui keeps a local structural mirror of the request-snapshot section-tag type ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "RequestSectionTag",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " / "
        },
        {
          "insert": "RequestSectionKind",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "detail-panel/renderers/turn-sections.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") rather than importing the canonical type from "
        },
        {
          "insert": "@agent-kernel/protocol",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "PiRequestSnapshotData",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). The shapes are intentionally identical, and snapshots without tags parse to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "null",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " so the renderer falls back to the flat context list.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": viewer-ui must stay buildable against protocol versions that predate the field. Importing the protocol type directly (the rejected alternative) couples viewer-ui builds to protocol version.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "detail-panel/renderers/turn-sections.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and any future viewer type mirroring an optional protocol field."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-decision-viewer-com-21": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-decision-viewer-com-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Viewer components are vertical slices: a folder named for the component with a thin index composition root and responsibility-named siblings; external import specifiers resolve through the folder index, so restructuring is invisible to consumers. Single-responsibility modules stay flat files. folderizing for symmetry is an anti-pattern.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": The alternative, shared-by-layer folders ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "components/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "hooks/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "utils/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), scatters one component's parts and makes deletion unsafe.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent-viewer/AgentCatalogViewer/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (the exemplar) and every new multi-file component."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-00-overview-decision-prompt-ren-22": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-decision-prompt-ren-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Prompt-rendering surfaces build on prompt-kit's shared editor surface: the editor tokens are defined once in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "@codecaine-ai/prompt-kit",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "ui/surface/editor-surface.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), and the inline lab ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "PromptInlineLab",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") is re-exported from prompt-kit rather than reimplemented; viewer-ui adds the kernel-facing shells ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "AgentCatalogViewer",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "AgentPromptLabContainer",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "RevisionHistoryPanel",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "RevisionStatsStrip",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ").\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Every prompt view sharing one token source is what keeps views from drifting (prompt-kit's presentation contract); a viewer-local token copy or lab fork (rejected) would drift on the first edit.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent-viewer/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and any new prompt-rendering surface."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
