    "b-00-overview-lab-data-flow": {
      "id": "b-00-overview-lab-data-flow",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The lab's views, zones, and editing behavior are prompt-kit's, documented in the prompt-kit repo's UI implementation doc (docs/30-implementation/10-prompt-kit/20-ui). The kernel side is the data feeding it. Context fixtures flow from "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/kernel/src/context-fixtures.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " through "
        },
        {
          "insert": "catalog-service.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " into "
        },
        {
          "insert": "CatalogAgentDetail.contextFixtures",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". "
        },
        {
          "insert": "AgentPromptLabContainer",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " passes them to the lab's fixture picker unless the host supplies its own context preview. The Tools view document comes from the host's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "toolsZone",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " when set. Otherwise "
        },
        {
          "insert": "render-tools.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " renders the selected context fixture's tools, falling back to the detail's tool preview ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "CatalogAgentDetail.tools",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). When the host enables editing, prompt annotations open prompt-edit sessions on the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "KERNEL_PROMPT_EDIT_SESSION_PATHS",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " routes, and the controller follows session events over SSE."
        }
      ],
